  "ownsLevel": {
    "confidence": "verified",
    "items": [
      "Changing `DLC2ExpSpiderFireCloaking` 017077 also needs `DLC2ExpSpiderFireCloakingFriend` 019529 (friendly twin, level 12): it uses 017077 as its template but not for `Stats`. Likewise `DLC2ExpSpiderFrostCloaking` 0206E1 → `DLC2ExpSpiderFrostCloakingFriend` 0206DC (level 12), `DLC2ExpSpiderPoisonCloaking` 01CAAD → `DLC2ExpSpiderPoisonCloakingFriend` 01CAAE (level 12) and `DLC2ExpSpiderShockCloaking` 02095C → `DLC2ExpSpiderShockCloakingFriend` 02095D (level 12). All :Dragonborn.esm; the twins are scroll summons, on Conjured → Summoned Creatures → *Constructs & Dragons*.",
      "The Jumping spiders' level owner is `DLC2ExpSpiderTemplate` 014490:Dragonborn.esm (\"Imbued Spider\", PcLevelMult 1, no template, not placed). Changing it also moves every spider that carries `Stats` from it: the Fire and Frost Jumping Friend twins `DLC2ExpSpiderFireJumpingFriend` 014491 and `DLC2ExpSpiderFrostJumpingFriend` 0206DD (scroll summons), the Poison and Shock Jumping spiders and their twins, `DLC2ExpSpiderZombieFriend`, and the placed Albino copy `DLC2ExpSpiderAlbinoEMPTY` (see *Albino Spider*).",
      "Two more spiders use 014490 as their template but keep their own level: `DLC2ExpSpiderShockCloaking` 02095C (level 6, a row) and the scroll summon `DLC2ExpSpiderOilFriend` 02749A (PcLevelMult 1, on *Constructs & Dragons*). The Glowing and Pack spiders are never in game (see *Insectoids*).",
      "`DLC2ExpSpiderOil`: no other record keeps its own level.",
      "The spider-zombie hosts follow the bandit ladder; the records that keep their own level beside it are on *Common Bandits*."
    ]
  },
